39,2,1,talk,Midori,,"It seems my concerns were justified. I found that a previous joint clinic failed because neither department would take responsibility for the budget or the rota, and shared nursing rounds suffered significant visit losses.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,1,talk,Jonathan,,"My findings are equally sobering. A previous call-back trial significantly reduced readmissions for elderly patients, but the effect vanished once it stopped. Also, the booking system ignores any work without a fixed appointment.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,1,talk,Misaki,,"The staffing situation is precarious. Ward nursing vacancies are high and agency costs are rising, but interestingly, the midwifery rota has unusual slack due to falling birth numbers.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,1,talk,Shion,,"The financial outlook is grim. The development allocation is down by nearly a quarter, and we're now paying for floor space out of that same budget. Furthermore, off-site contacts bring in no regional fund tariffs.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,1,talk,Shizue,,"I've discovered that our outpatient rooms and parking are nearly full by mid-morning, and our shuttle only reaches a few villages. Also, getting data agreements with outside surgeries is a very slow process.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Midori,,"@Shion, if off-site contacts bring in no tariffs and the budget is shrinking, we must be very careful about any program that relies on home visits or external coordination.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,2,talk,Jonathan,,"I agree with Midori. If the booking system doesn't even record non-appointment work, any program relying on informal coordination will be invisible and likely unfunded in the long run.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,2,talk,Misaki,,"That makes me worry about the nursing staff. If we add a program that requires a lot of unrecorded work, the already strained ward nurses will be the ones feeling the pressure.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,2,talk,Shion,,"Precisely. If we choose a program that generates no revenue and consumes a shrinking budget, we are simply setting it up for failure. We need something that fits the current financial reality.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,2,talk,Shizue,,"I am also concerned. If the parking and rooms are already full, any program that brings more people onto the site will only add to the congestion and stress for our patients.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Midori,,"@Misaki, you mentioned the midwifery rota has some slack. Perhaps we should look for a program that utilizes that specific capacity rather than adding to the ward nurses' burden.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,3,talk,Jonathan,,"That is a logical pivot. If we can find a program that leverages existing slack rather than creating new gaps, we might actually sustain it.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,3,talk,Misaki,,I agree. Using the midwifery capacity would be much more sustainable than trying to squeeze more out of the ward nurses who are already relying on agency cover.,"{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,3,talk,Shion,,"It's a rare opportunity to find a resource that isn't already overstretched. If we can align that slack with a program that doesn't drain the development budget or require expensive new floor space, we might have a viable option.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,3,talk,Shizue,,"I agree. If we can find a program that doesn't require more rooms or complex data agreements with outside surgeries, it would be much easier for the hospital to absorb.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Midori,,"I think we have a clear set of criteria now: we need a program that utilizes the midwifery slack, avoids adding to the ward nursing burden, and doesn't overstretch our physical space or budget.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
55,2,4,talk,Jonathan,,I agree. We should prioritize a program that is administratively simple and doesn't rely on the invisible work that our booking system fails to capture.,"{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
56,2,4,talk,Misaki,,"I'll support any option that protects the ward staff. If we can shift the focus to the midwifery team, we avoid the risk of further burnout and agency reliance.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
57,2,4,talk,Shion,,"I'll agree for now. As long as the program doesn't require a massive upfront investment in floor space or rely on non-existent tariffs, it might actually survive its first year.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
58,2,4,talk,Shizue,,I agree. Let us hope the candidates include something that fits these constraints without causing more stress for our staff or patients.,"{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
